# Aura Store: what belongs in the repository.
#
# The repository holds the app, its README, its licence and the licence of the font it ships.
# Everything else on this machine is either generated by a build, specific to this machine, or a
# record of a working session.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets and signing material
#
# Nothing in this section may ever be committed. A keystore is the app's identity: with it, anyone
# can sign an update that Android accepts as this app. local.properties names that keystore and
# carries its passwords, and it is also the file Gradle reads the SDK path from.
local.properties
local.properties.*
**/local.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pkcs12
*.pem
*.key
*.pepk
*.asc
*.gpg
*.bks
*.jceks
*.truststore
app/keystore/
keystore/
keystores/
signing/
secrets.properties
seystore.properties
*.env
*.env.*
.env
.envrc
google-services.json
firebase-service-account*.json
service-account*.json
.ssh/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the other shapes a secret takes
#
# A key is not always a keystore. These are the names the tools that hold credentials use, and the
# names they use for a copy of one: a base64 blob of the signing key, a token file for a service, a
# registry login that a command line reads without asking.
*.jks.base64
*.keystore.base64
*.p12.base64
*.base64
secrets.json
secrets.yml
secrets.yaml
secret.json
secret.yml
secret.yaml
secrets.token
credentials.json
credentials.yml
credentials.yaml
client_secret*.json
*-service-account.json
gcloud-*.json
application_default_credentials.json
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform/
.netrc
_netrc
*.netrc
.pgpass
pgpass
.git-credentials
.npmrc
.pypirc
.dockercfg
.docker/config.json
.cargo/credentials.toml
*.kdbx
*.kdb
*.keychain
*.agilekeychain
mcp.json
mcp_settings.json
.github/secrets.yml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- private keys by their own names
#
# A key that lives outside a keystore is a key all the same. The bare names are here because a
# clone that lands in the wrong folder carries them with it.
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_dsa
id_dsa.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*.ppk
*.ovpn

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Gradle and the Android build
.gradle/
.kotlin/
build/
app/build/
captures/
*.apk
*.aab
*.aar
*.ap_
*.dex
*.hprof
gradle/gradle-daemon-jvm.properties
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- what a device hands back
#
# A file pulled off a handset is the app's own data: the queue holds signed download links, a
# database holds the installed list, and a trace holds whatever the screen was showing. None of it
# belongs in a public tree.
*.obb
*.apks
*.vdex
*.odex
*.art
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*-journal
*-wal
*-shm
shared_prefs*.xml
*_queue.xml
*.trace
*.perfetto-trace
trace/
traces/
perfetto/
perfetto-trace
*.log
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- IDE and OS files
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.bak
*~
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Documentation: the README is the
# only document this repository ships. The rest of the writing lives with the working sessions.
#
# The four guides under /docs/ are the published part: how the project is put together, how a
# change is made, how a release is built, and what the prose gate is. The session notes, the
# archive and the design write-ups stay with the sessions that wrote them.
/docs/CONTINUATION*.md
/docs/SESSION_*.md
/docs/AUDIT_AND_FIXES.md
/docs/NAVBAR_SETTINGS.md
/docs/PORTING_LIQUID_GLASS.md
/CONTINUATION.md
/HANDOFF.md
/PROBLEM_ANALYSIS.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The agent harness's own files. The
# instructions it runs under and the skills it loads are machine-local: the repository ships the
# linter the prose gate needs (tools/anti-ai-slop), not the agent's copies of it.
/AGENTS.md
/.agents/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Screenshots, UI dumps, verification
# runs and backups from working sessions. The README keeps its own small set under /media/.
/shots/
/screenshots/
/logo/explore/
/u*.xml
/ui.xml
/verify/
/verify_*/
/_audit/
/_backup_*/
/.perch/
/.freebuff/
*.orig
*.rej

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Python caches for the checker tools
# and the vendored prose skill
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Scaffolding from tooling that no
# build reads
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules/
